    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d171">

                <pb facs="0294" n="128" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg128"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/1756</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Continental and Commercial Trust
                            &amp; Savings Bank to the Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chicago, Illinois</hi></placeName>, <lb/>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-14T18:30:00-06:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 14, 1917, 6.30 p.m</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In connection with the loan negotiations which this bank has been conducting with
                    the Republic of China through Minister Koo, we have requested an extention of
                    time until June 15 in which to send our representatives to China to make a full
                    investigation and conduct the negotiations. While we understand Minister Koo has
                    requested the extention we have received no advice that his request has been
                    granted. We would be much pleased if you would take the matter up with the
                    American Minister at Peking and endeavor to secure the extension for us.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Arthur Reynold</hi>, <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Vice President</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
